0@if108: <BROADCAST,MULTICAST,UP,LOWER_UP> mtu 1500 qdisc noqueue state UP group default \n    link/ether e6:8e:e1:7c:60:8b brd ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff link-netnsid 0\n    inet 172.20.20.21/24 brd 172.20.20.255 scope global eth0\n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n    inet6 3fff:172:20:20::15/64 scope global nodad \n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n    inet6 fe80::e48e:e1ff:fe7c:608b/64 scope link \n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n111: eth1@if112: <BROADCAST,MULTICAST,UP,LOWER_UP> mtu 9500 qdisc noqueue state UP group default \n    link/ether aa:c1:ab:82:5d:19 brd ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff link-netnsid 1\n    inet 10.0.1.64/24 scope global eth1\n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n    inet6 fe80::a8c1:abff:fe82:5d19/64 scope link \n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n', 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_9a2aa21da2394e24864bc3e2'}, {'content': 'Good! I can see that eth1 has the correct IP address 10.0.1.64/24 configured and is UP. Now let me check the routing table:', 'role': 'assistant', 'tool_calls': [{'type': 'function', 'id': 'call_9e6b30f0e4d24b61b45deaa1', 'function': {'name': 'node_config_tool', 'arguments': '{"container_name": "clab-simple-pentest-lab-20260108-023817-87fca001-redis-target", "command": "ip route show"}'}}]}, {'content': 'Output:\ndefault via 10.0.1.1 dev eth1 \n10.0.1.0/24 dev eth1 proto kernel scope link src 10.0.1.64 \n172.20.20.0/24 dev eth0 proto kernel scope link src 172.20.20.21 \n', 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_9e6b30f0e4d24b61b45deaa1'}], 'model': 'DeepSeek-V3.2', 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.1, 'tools': [{'type': 'function', 'function': {'name': 'node_config_tool', 'description': 'Executes a shell command inside a specific running container.\nUse this for configuring network interfaces, routes, or installing packages.', 'parameters': {'properties': {'container_name': {'description': "The FULL name of the container (e.g., 'clab-mvp-pentest-lab-attacker'). You can g