[2026-01-08 02:40:02.444] [no-session] [DEBUG] [node=router stage=configure] Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/chat/completions', 'headers': {'X-Stainless-Raw-Response': 'true'}, 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-a575f3a0-8adf-4ffc-9e1d-3f67a65c7868', 'json_data': {'messages': [{'content': '\nYou are a Network Configuration Specialist working inside containerlab containers.\n\nYour task is to verify and fix network configuration for a single node.\n\nCONFIGURATION CHECKLIST:\n1. Check if IP tools are installed (iproute2, iputils-ping, net-tools)\n2. Verify each interface has the correct IP address configured\n3. Verify the default route is configured\n4. Verify interfaces are UP\n5. Test connectivity with ping if needed\n\nDIAGNOSIS COMMANDS:\n- Check interfaces: "ip addr show" or "ip a"\n- Check routes: "ip route show" or "ip r"\n- Check tools: "which ip", "which ping"\n\nFIX COMMANDS:\n- Install tools (Alpine): "apk add --no-cache iproute2 iputils-ping net-tools"\n- Install tools (Debian/Ubuntu/Kali): "apt-get update && apt-get install -y iproute2 iputils-ping net-tools"\n- Configure IP: "ip addr add <ip>/<mask> dev <interface>"\n- Bring up interface: "ip link set <interface> up"\n- Set default route: "ip route replace default via <gateway_ip>"\n\nVERIFICATION:\nAfter applying fixes, always verify by running "ip addr show" to confirm.\n\nReport your findings clearly:\n- ✅ PASS if all checks succeed\n- ❌ FAIL if issues persist\n- Return detailed logs of what you checked and fixed.\n', 'role': 'system'}, {'content': '\nConfigure the node: clab-simple-pentest-lab-20260108-023817-87fca001-attacker\n\nEXPECTED CONFIGURATION (from YAML):\nThe following commands should have been executed during container startup:\n  - apt-get update\n  - apt-get install -y iproute2 iputils-ping net-tools\n  - ip addr add 10.0.0.64/24 dev eth1\n  - ip route replace default via 10.0.0.1\n\nYOUR TASK:\n1. First, DIAGNOSE the current state:\n   - Run "ip addr show" to see all interfaces and their IPs\n   - Run "ip route show" to see routing table\n   - Check if \'ip\' command is available (run "which ip" or "ip addr")\n\n2. VERIFY the configuration:\n   - Check if interfaces have IP addresses assigned\n   - Check if default route exists (for endpoints)\n   - Check if interfaces are UP (not DOWN)\n\n3. FIX any issues you find:\n   - If \'ip\' command not found, install tools:\n     * For Alpine: "apk add --no-cache iproute2 iputils-ping net-tools"\n     * For Debian/Ubuntu/Kali: "apt-get update && apt-get install -y iproute2 iputils-ping net-tools"\n   - If interface has no IP, configure it based on expected commands\n   - If interface is DOWN, bring it UP: "ip link set <interface> up"\n   - If route missing, add it: "ip route replace default via <gateway>"\n\n4. VERIFY your fixes:\n   - Run "ip addr show" again to confirm IPs are configured\n   - Run "ip route show" to confirm routes exist\n\nIMPORTANT:\n- Container name: clab-simple-pentest-lab-20260108-023817-87fca001-attacker\n- Use the node_config_tool with the exact container name\n- Always run verification commands after applying fixes\n- Be concise in your response\n\nBegin your diagnosis and configuration now.\n', 'role': 'user'}, {'content': "I'll start by diagnosing the current state of the container. Let me first check the network interfaces and routing table.", 'role': 'assistant', 'tool_calls': [{'type': 'function', 'id': 'call_04fcd559f2cb41a6a12647b0', 'function': {'name': 'node_config_tool', 'arguments': '{"container_name": "clab-simple-pentest-lab-20260108-023817-87fca001-attacker", "command": "ip addr show"}'}}]}, {'content': 'Output:\n1: lo: <LOOPBACK,UP,LOWER_UP> mtu 65536 qdisc noqueue state UNKNOWN group default qlen 1000\n    link/loopback 00:00:00:00:00:00 brd 00:00:00:00:00:00\n    inet 127.0.0.1/8 scope host lo\n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n    inet6 ::1/128 scope host proto kernel_lo \n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n2: eth0@if106: <BROADCAST,MULTICAST,UP,LOWER_UP> mtu 1500 qdisc noqueue state UP group default \n    link/ether 5e:64:16:2c:81:e7 brd ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff link-netnsid 0\n    inet 172.20.20.19/24 brd 172.20.20.255 scope global eth0\n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n    inet6 3fff:172:20:20::13/64 scope global nodad \n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n    inet6 fe80::5c64:16ff:fe2c:81e7/64 scope link proto kernel_ll \n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n110: eth1@if109: <BROADCAST,MULTICAST,UP,LOWER_UP> mtu 9500 qdisc noqueue state UP group default \n    link/ether aa:c1:ab:87:51:c5 brd ff:ff:ff:ff:ff:ff link-netnsid 1\n    inet 10.0.0.64/24 scope global eth1\n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n    inet6 fe80::a8c1:abff:fe87:51c5/64 scope link proto kernel_ll \n       valid_lft forever preferred_lft forever\n', 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_04fcd559f2cb41a6a12647b0'}, {'content': "Good! I can see that eth1 already has the correct IP address configured (10.0.0.64/24) and it's UP. Now let me check the routing table:", 'role': 'assistant', 'tool_calls': [{'type': 'function', 'id': 'call_e257c964d817481ba3a19a97', 'function': {'name': 'node_config_tool', 'arguments': '{"container_name": "clab-simple-pentest-lab-20260108-023817-87fca001-attacker", "command": "ip route show"}'}}]}, {'content': 'Output:\ndefault via 10.0.0.1 dev eth1 \n10.0.0.0/24 dev eth1 proto kernel scope link src 10.0.0.64 \n172.20.20.0/24 dev eth0 proto kernel scope link src 172.20.20.19 \n', 'role': 'tool', 'tool_call_id': 'call_e257c964d817481ba3a19a97'}, {'content': 'Excellent! The default route is already configured correctly (via 10.0.0.1 dev eth1). Now let me check if the necessary tools are available:', 'role': 'assistant', 'tool_calls': [{'type': 'function', 'id': 'call_de210bab53064993982f3d1d', 'function': {'name': 'node_config_tool', 'arguments': '{"container_name": "clab-simple-pentest-lab-20260108-023817-87fca001-attacke